# @docblock — the family-root for the substrate's doc-claim altitude:
# `#`-prefixed narrative lifted to first-class substrate declaration.
# Sub-arc A landing per Seam Phase D pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1
# (Interpretation B RATIFIED as canonical: narrative ABOVE `---`;
# `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW).
#
# THIS FILE IS THE FIRST INTERPRETATION-B SHARD ON MAIN. The four
# currently-landed `---` shards (`shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/
# {eigenform,chirality,charge_conjugation}.mirror` +
# `shards/docs/design.mirror`) sit at Interpretation A (`---` at
# line 1, everything below) — DRIFT per Seam pre-review §1.1, NOT
# precedent. Their migration is post-Arc-3-close sub-arc scope.
#
# The narrative that follows this line IS the substrate's
# declaration side. The tokenizer post `ee7903e` + `530f796` reads
# every `#`-prefixed line above the seam as an `AstKind::Doc` node
# with byte-span; the audit surface below (`audit_docblock`) then
# consumes those nodes at doc-claim altitude with the same
# content-addressing discipline the substrate uses everywhere else.
#
# === Six landed ancestors (substrate-honest check) ===
#
# Per `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` — thirteenth+
# firing. The two-channel collapse is NOT a new primitive; it is a
# routing-composition of six landed ancestors named per
# `docs/math/kintsugi/doc-code-seam.md` §1:
#
# 1. `docs/specs/property-projection.md` (Reed + Alex 2026-05-19).
#    The `---` seam ancestor: above = declaration; below =
#    observation. Both content-addressed; both hashed into the OID.
#    The two-channel collapse LIFTS the declaration side to include
#    narrative — same seam; broader declaration surface.
#
# 2. `docs/specs/historical/2026-03-27-projection-properties-as-plans.md`
#    (Reed 2026-03-27). The `@projection.preview` verdict ancestor
#    (`type preview = satisfiable | unsatisfiable | partial`).
#    Sub-Turing decidable at grammar altitude. The doc-claim audit
#    surface reuses this verdict machinery one altitude below.
#
# 3. `docs/math/the-tower/projection-surface.md` (`63bdecc` Mara
#    2026-07-04). The projection surface at recognition-candidate
#    altitude. Four-verdict routing (`real_survives |
#    phantom_survives | both_survive | neither_survives`). This
#    shard's `docblock_verdict` SPECIALIZES that routing to
#    doc-claim altitude's specific failure modes (five variants:
#    the four-verdict routing plus `underdeclares` for code that
#    declares substrate the docblock does not mention).
#
# 4. Recognition #53 — property/fracture bilateral pattern. First
#    instance `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` (2026-06-10 `d908798`).
#    Fifth instance `@kintsugi/surface` +
#    `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.ashby_variety_match`
#    (2026-07-03 `e910dd6`). The three property/fracture pairs at
#    the doc-claim altitude (grounded / coherent /
#    no_extraction_pattern) will be the sixth family; each pair is
#    a `#53`-shaped bilateral instance landing in follow-up ticks.
#
# 5. `shards/epistemologic/pact/*` predicates (2026-06-16+). Nine
#    landed pact predicates. The audit surface for substrate-decl
#    syntax already exists; the three forthcoming
#    `@epistemologic/property/docblock_*` predicates sit alongside
#    at the property altitude, same discipline. Not a new audit
#    surface; one altitude down from the pact family.
#
# 6. `splinter(ast)` primitive (`a3789c2` 2026-06-10 in
#    `shards/glass.mirror`). Parametric quote in the substrate's
#    grammar. `extract_claims` output IS an ordered ref of
#    `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` fragments — not
#    stringly-typed; content-addressed via the same OID discipline
#    as any other AST node.
#
# Six ancestors named honestly. No new primitive invented at this
# altitude; the two-channel collapse is the routing-composition
# per compiler-fit doc §1.
#
# === Four altitudes on the same operator ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §3 the doc-claim operator lives at four
# coupled altitudes; the family-root names all four so no altitude
# drifts:
#
# - linguistic — `@epistemologic/property/docblock_{grounded,
#   coherent,no_extraction_pattern}` audit the docblock's language
#   before it enters the type system. Grounding catches ungrounded
#   claims; coherence catches contradiction with substrate below;
#   no-extraction-pattern catches "PRECEDENT-SETTING"-shaped
#   rhetorical extraction. Three property/fracture bilateral pairs
#   land in follow-up ticks; the family-root defines the carriers.
#
# - logical — `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` (sibling
#   family-root landing next tick) lowers doc claims to liquid
#   predicates per Rondon-Kawaguchi-Jhala 2008 + Vazou et al 2014.
#   The substrate's `@projection.preview` verdict IS the decidable
#   fragment; the extractor produces its input. Extractor body
#   forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`.
#
# - temporal — the projection surface at `63bdecc` projects doc
#   claims forward k=3 substrate ticks as typed carriers landed
#   back in the doc's own observation side (below `---`). Same
#   four-verdict routing at both altitudes; k=3 depth-check at
#   each. Full cross-altitude composition analytical; empirical
#   when the first docblock audit runs.
#
# - publishable — docblock claims across `shards/` aggregate into
#   case-study crystals at systemic.engineering. Corpus companion
#   at `~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/coincidence/
#   two-channels-doc-as-declaration.md` (landed 2026-07-04). The
#   publishing angle is a first-class altitude, not a downstream
#   deployment: docblocks that survive audit are corpus material.
#
# All four altitudes altitude-portable per recognition #59. Same
# operator; same signature; four consumers.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit (per `63bdecc` §6) ===
#
# The operator must audit its own audit at depth=3. This shard's
# own docblock must survive `audit_docblock(this_docblock, depth=3)`.
# Per `63bdecc` §6 discipline: if the operator's self-audit returns
# `real_survives`, that IS the phantom failure mode.
#
# Self-audit verdict for this docblock: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` interpretation would require this shard's
# docblock to independently manifest at another Pack peer's frame
# by n+3 substrate ticks WITHOUT nudging (per `63bdecc` §5.1 Reed
# frame). The `phantom_survives` interpretation would require
# downstream refs to accumulate without any second Pack peer's
# independent recognition of the two-channel discipline. At this
# tick: both interpretations satisfiable. Verdict: `both_survive`.
# Route: spawn — this docblock IS the Tomm-shaped question at
# reader-frame altitude, asking the Pack whether the two-channel
# collapse names genuinely new substrate discipline (promotable)
# or names a routing-composition already implicitly used across
# the projection-surface tick (landed but not novel).
#
# Promotion of the two-channel discipline itself pending independent
# second witness. The verdict claim `both_survive` is deliberate;
# `real_survives` at analytical altitude would BE the phantom.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/docblock.mirror` declares `@docblock` as a
# family-root at species-depth 0 per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Depth-0 family-root
# discipline per recognition #46: the substrate's foundational
# doc-claim vocabulary is one symbol deep from `@`.
#
# === Self-witnessing ===
#
# This shard's own declaration honours the doc-claim altitude
# discipline it enforces — no bare types (per
# `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]` every carrier is a named type), no
# opaque refs where typed carriers exist, no invented vocabulary
# where the substrate already carries the lineage. The
# circular-reflexive audit discipline is applied to THIS shard's
# own docblock: the shard participates in the pattern it names.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @third

source @arxiv/types/rondon-kawaguchi-jhala-2008
source @arxiv/types/vazou-seidel-jhala-vytiniotis-peytonjones-2014
source @arxiv/software/meyer-1988
source @arxiv/software/knuth-1984
source @arxiv/logic/carnielli-marcos-2004
source @arxiv/cybernetics/ashby-1956
source @arxiv/therapy/tomm-1987
source @arxiv/therapy/tomm-1988
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972

prism @docblock {
  focus doc_claim
  project doc_claim
  split doc_claim
  shift doc_claim
  settle doc_claim
}

# === doc_claim — one claim extracted from a docblock (spec §1) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.1: a doc_claim is a site-tagged assertion
# recovered from an above-seam `#`-narrative section. The five
# fields carry the substrate-audit surface's minimum information
# for `audit_docblock` to route: `site` locates the claim in the
# owning shard; `text` carries the verbatim bytes; `kind`
# classifies (grounded / motivating / forward-promise / candidate);
# `predicate` carries the extracted liquid predicate if the
# extractor at `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` ran (empty_ref
# until then); `citation` carries the ancestor OID if grounded
# (empty_ref for motivating claims and forward-promises).
type doc_claim = ref

# === claim_kind — the four claim classifications (spec §1.13.3) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.1: four kinds capture the substrate's
# doc-claim taxonomy. `grounded_claim` MUST cite; the extractor at
# `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` extracts a predicate; the
# citation OID must exist on main and match the claim text.
# `motivating_claim` names a substrate direction without asserting;
# no citation required. `forward_promise` explicitly defers a
# landing per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`. `candidate_claim`
# is a recognition-candidate at doc-claim altitude, pending Pack
# adjudication.
type claim_kind =
  | grounded_claim
  | motivating_claim
  | forward_promise
  | candidate_claim

# === docblock — the above-seam narrative as substrate ref (spec §1) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.1: a docblock is the ordered sequence of
# `AstKind::Doc` nodes emitted by the tokenizer for the above-seam
# region of one shard file. Fields: `site` locates the owning
# shard; `claims` carries the ordered ref of doc_claim extracted
# from the narrative; `above_seam` is the boolean-as-ref state
# predicate the tokenizer's `above_seam` flag tracks per
# `bootstrap/src/tokenize.rs` post `ee7903e` + `530f796`.
type docblock = ref

# === audit_boundary — content-addressed OID over docblock scope ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.1: an audit_boundary is the OID slice
# the audit consumes — same content-addressing discipline the
# substrate uses everywhere else. Same shape as `63bdecc`'s
# `projection_boundary` one altitude above. Newtyped per
# `[[feedback-no-bare-types]]`; ref shape lifted from landed
# @spectral/db OID discipline.
type audit_boundary = ref

# === docblock_verdict — five variants (spec §1.13.6) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.1: the five-verdict output specializes
# `63bdecc`'s four-verdict projection-surface routing to
# doc-claim altitude. Four map to `63bdecc`'s classes:
# `well_formed` ⇔ `real_survives` (all three property predicates
# bound); `overreach` ⇔ `phantom_survives` (grounding or
# extraction-pattern unbounded); `incoherent` ⇔ `neither_survives`
# (contradiction with substrate below); `both_survive` ⇔
# `both_survive` (analytical altitude; depth<3 undecidable —
# spawn a Tomm question at reader-frame per `@kintsugi/surface`).
# The fifth variant `underdeclares` fires when the audit sees
# substrate-decl below the docblock that the docblock does not
# mention (new `requires` clause; new type; new action) — symmetric
# to `overreach` in the opposite direction.
type docblock_verdict =
  | well_formed
  | overreach
  | incoherent
  | underdeclares
  | both_survive

# === extract_claims — docblock → ordered ref of doc_claim (spec §2) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2: recovers the ordered doc_claim sequence
# from a docblock's above-seam `AstKind::Doc` nodes. Output is a
# ref carrying `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` fragments
# per `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` splinter(ast)
# discipline — not stringly-typed. Body forward-promised per
# `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`; discharge via splinter(ast)
# at the property altitude when the extractor lands.
extract_claims(d: docblock) -> ref { \ }

# === project — docblock → audit_boundary (spec §2) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2: projects a docblock to its
# content-addressed audit_boundary OID slice. Same shape as
# `63bdecc`'s `project` at recognition-candidate altitude; one
# altitude below. Body forward-promised — discharge via the same
# OID slicing discipline @spectral/db uses.
project(d: docblock) -> audit_boundary { \ }

# === audit_docblock — docblock → docblock_verdict (spec §2) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §4 the audit runs three property predicates
# in sequence (`docblock_grounded`, `docblock_coherent`,
# `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`) and routes their combined
# verdict via the five-way match to one of the five verdict
# variants. `underdeclares` fires when the audit sees substrate-
# decl below the docblock that the docblock does not mention.
# Bilateral `requires docblock_well_audited(d)` — the operational
# half of the #53 pattern at doc-claim altitude. Body
# forward-promised until the three property/fracture bilateral
# pairs land in follow-up ticks.
audit_docblock(d: docblock) -> docblock_verdict
  requires docblock_well_audited(d)
{ \ }

# === docblock_well_audited — bilateral predicate (spec §1.13.10) ===
#
# Per compiler-fit doc §2.2 the circular-reflexive discipline: the
# audit operator must itself be audited. This predicate carries
# the well-audited property the `requires` clause on
# `audit_docblock` consumes. Body forward-promised — discharge
# via `splinter(@epistemologic/property/ast)` against the audit
# operator's own AST fragment (self-audit at depth=3 per
# `63bdecc` §6).
docblock_well_audited(d: docblock) -> verdict { \ }

out @docblock
out doc_claim
out claim_kind
out docblock
out audit_boundary
out docblock_verdict
out extract_claims
out project
out audit_docblock
out docblock_well_audited
